            <ArticleTitle>Persistent postpartum headache from a chronic subdural hematoma after peridural anesthesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>808-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Postpartum headache after peridural anesthesia is usually attributed to accidental perforation of the dura causing postlumbar puncture headache.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">In a patient with persistent headache after peridural anesthesia for labor, a chronic subdural hematoma was diagnosed 5 weeks postpartum.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Caution is warranted in patients with peridural anesthesia for labor who present with unusually persistent headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
